What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_powerY_energy
KernelVersion:	7.3
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Energy in microjoules accumulated by the rail on channel Y since
		the driver last started the meter, as an unsigned 64-bit count.

		The meter integrates in hardware, and the driver carries the
		total across the latches it performs, so the difference between
		two reads is the energy the rail used in between however long
		that was and however few times it was read. Reading this
		attribute latches the meter, which is what keeps the total
		current; the total only ever grows, so concurrent readers do
		not take measurements away from one another.

		A window whose sample count is not consistent with the time it
		spanned is not added to the total, and is counted in
		lost_windows instead.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/lost_windows
KernelVersion:	7.3
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Number of measurement windows the driver discarded because they
		could not be trusted, as an unsigned count.

		A window is discarded when its sample count disagrees with the
		time the window spanned, which happens when the meter's counter
		has saturated -- it spans about 2.3 hours at the programmed
		sample rate and cannot be restarted once full -- or when reading
		the accumulators failed part way through. The meter is restarted
		when this happens, so the counter advancing across an interval
		means that interval's energy is incomplete and should be shown
		as a gap rather than as a low number.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_powerY_suspend_energy
KernelVersion:	7.3
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		The part of in_powerY_energy that was measured across a system
		sleep, in microjoules.

		The driver closes the measurement window as the system suspends
		and again as it resumes, and adds the window in between to this
		total only if the system did suspend: a cycle that aborted
		before sleeping is ordinary awake time and is left out.

		The window is bounded by the driver's own suspend and resume
		callbacks rather than by the sleep, so it also contains the
		device suspend and resume either side of it. Divide by
		suspend_time_us, which counts the elapsed time of exactly these
		windows, rather than by a sleep length measured elsewhere.
		Subtracting this total from in_powerY_energy over an interval
		leaves what the rail used while the system was running.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/suspend_time_us
KernelVersion:	7.3
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Total elapsed time, in microseconds, of the windows counted in
		in_powerY_suspend_energy. It is the denominator that belongs
		with that numerator: their ratio is a true mean power, where a
		sleep duration measured elsewhere would not cover the same
		interval.
